# One line-ending convention on every platform. The oracle harness pins files by
# hash (the lock file, the corpus manifest, the golden observations), so the same
# bytes must come out of a checkout on Windows and on Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Game records of our own are pinned by the hash of their bytes (the manifest in
# oracles/corpus/), and some oracles are sensitive to line endings: git must hand
# them back exactly as they were committed.
oracles/corpus/records/** -text
